import json
R=[
("Q390904","Luc-Olivier Merson was a French painter born in Paris in 1846. He won the Prix de Rome in 1869 with his picture of the runner of Marathon, then taught at the École des Beaux-Arts and also designed banknotes and stamps. He lived and worked in Paris until he died in 1920."),
("Q604107","Wilhelm von Kaulbach was a German painter born in Arolsen in 1805. He worked in Munich, where he became head of the art academy and painted huge murals of history and legend for the king of Bavaria. He died in Munich in 1874."),
("Q561205","Raphael was an Italian painter born in Urbino in 1483. He worked in Florence and then in Rome, where he painted the Vatican's famous rooms, and with Leonardo and Michelangelo he is counted among the three giants of the High Renaissance. He died in Rome in 1520 at the age of only 37."),
("Q718975","François-André Vincent was a French painter born in Paris in 1746. He won the Prix de Rome, studied in Italy and became a leading history painter in the Neoclassical style, a rival of Jacques-Louis David. He taught at the art academy in Paris and died there in 1816."),
("Q250194","Anselm Feuerbach was a German painter born in Speyer in 1829. He studied in Düsseldorf, Munich and Paris and lived for many years in Italy, where he painted calm scenes from classical antiquity. He died in Venice in 1880."),
("Q1342328","Michiel Sweerts was a Flemish painter born in Brussels in 1618. He worked in Rome, where he painted busy city scenes, and later in Brussels and Amsterdam, before joining a missionary journey to Asia. He died in Goa, India, in 1664."),
("Q5598","Rembrandt van Rijn was born in Leiden in 1606 and moved to Amsterdam in 1631, where he became the most famous painter in Holland. He painted portraits, Bible stories and over eighty self-portraits, and went bankrupt later in life. He died in Amsterdam in 1669."),
("Q2559361","Jean-François Pierre Peyron was a French painter born in Aix-en-Provence in 1744. He won the Prix de Rome, worked in Rome and became an important early Neoclassical history painter and later a director of the Gobelins tapestry works. He died in Paris in 1814."),
("Q153746","Albrecht Altdorfer was a German painter born near Nuremberg in about 1480 who lived in Regensburg, where he also served as a city councilor and architect. He was one of the first European artists to make landscapes the main subject of his pictures. He died in Regensburg in 1538."),
("Q271676","Charles Le Brun was a French painter born in Paris in 1619. He became First Painter to King Louis XIV and directed the decoration of the palace of Versailles and the Gobelins tapestry works. He died in Paris in 1690."),
("Q9440","Paolo Veronese was an Italian painter born in Verona in 1528. He moved to Venice, where he became famous for huge, colorful pictures of feasts and ceremonies full of costumes and architecture. He died in Venice in 1588."),
("Q333323","Pietro da Cortona was an Italian painter and architect born in the town of Cortona in 1596. He lived in Rome and became one of the leading artists of the Baroque, painting giant ceilings such as the one at the Palazzo Barberini. He died in Rome in 1669."),
("Q209050","Jan Brueghel the Elder was a Flemish painter born in Brussels in 1568, the son of the famous Pieter Bruegel the Elder. He lived in Antwerp, was a friend and partner of Rubens, and became known as 'Velvet' Brueghel for his soft, delicate paintings of landscapes and flowers. He died in Antwerp in 1625."),
("Q570172","Gaspar de Crayer was a Flemish painter born in Antwerp in 1584 who worked in Brussels and Ghent. He painted altarpieces and portraits in the Baroque style and was a respected rival of Rubens. He died in Ghent in 1669."),
("Q3174641","Jean-Simon Berthélemy was a French painter born in Laon in 1743. He worked in Paris, where he painted large history pictures for the royal court and, later, for the Revolution and Napoleon. He died in Paris in 1811."),
("Q1361950","Pietro Rotari was an Italian painter born in Verona in 1707. He painted portraits and charming scenes of young women, worked in Vienna and Dresden, and in 1756 moved to Saint Petersburg to paint at the court of Empress Elizabeth. He died there in 1762."),
("Q5599","Peter Paul Rubens was born in Siegen, Germany, in 1577 and grew up in Antwerp, which became his home. He was the most famous Baroque painter of northern Europe, ran a huge workshop, and also worked as a diplomat for Spain. He died in Antwerp in 1640."),
("Q3187562","Juan Antonio de Ribera was a Spanish painter born in Madrid in 1779. He studied in Paris under Jacques-Louis David and became a leading Neoclassical painter, later working for King Ferdinand VII of Spain. He died in Madrid in 1860."),
("Q689388","Franz Anton Maulbertsch was an Austrian painter born in Langenargen on Lake Constance in 1724. He lived in Vienna and became the greatest painter of the Austrian Rococo, famous for his colorful ceiling paintings in churches and palaces. He died in Vienna in 1796."),
("Q2555178","Nicolas Mignard was a French painter born in Troyes in 1606. He worked for many years in Avignon, where he was nicknamed Mignard of Avignon, and then moved to Paris to paint for the royal court. He was the older brother of the painter Pierre Mignard and died in Paris in 1668."),
("Q41554","Nicolas Poussin was a French painter born in Les Andelys in 1594. He moved to Rome as a young man and spent most of his life there, painting calm, well-planned scenes from ancient history and mythology that set the standard for classical painting. He died in Rome in 1665."),
("Q3340395","Nicolas-Guy Brenet was a French painter born in Paris in 1728. He studied in Rome and became a history painter, painting scenes from ancient and national history for the French royal court. He died in Paris in 1792."),
("Q17169","Giovanni Bellini was a Venetian painter, born in Venice around 1430 into a family of painters. He was the teacher of Giorgione and Titian and led Venetian painting into the High Renaissance with his glowing colors and quiet, thoughtful Madonnas. He worked in Venice all his life and died there in 1516."),
("Q75527","Heinrich Leutemann was a German painter and illustrator born near Leipzig in 1824. He was known for lively book illustrations of animals, travel and history, and lived in Leipzig and nearby Saxony. He died in 1905."),
("Q17325127","The Master of the Battle of Anghiari is the name given to an unknown Italian painter active in Florence around 1470. He is named after a painted chest panel of the Battle of Anghiari, and made colorful painted wooden chests that were given at weddings."),
("Q167220","Cornelis Cort was a Dutch engraver born in Hoorn in 1533. He moved to Venice and then Rome, where he made prints after famous paintings by Titian, Raphael and others, spreading their compositions across Europe. He died in Rome around 1575."),
("Q505758","Karl von Piloty was a German painter born in Munich in 1826. He became director of the Munich art academy and was famous for huge, dramatic scenes from history, which he taught to dozens of students. He died near Munich in 1886."),
("Q1056862","Cesare Maccari was an Italian painter born in Siena in 1840. He worked in Rome, where he painted large frescoes of ancient and national history, including one in the Italian Senate. He died in Rome in 1919."),
("Q1827276","Lionel Royer was a French painter born in Château-du-Loir in 1852. He studied in Paris and painted large pictures of French history and legend, which were popular in the years after France's defeat in the war of 1870. He died in Neuilly-sur-Seine in 1926."),
("Q938058","Jean Germain Drouais was a French painter born in Paris in 1763. He was a favorite pupil of Jacques-Louis David, won the Prix de Rome at 21, and became one of the most promising artists of his generation, but he died of smallpox in Rome in 1788 at the age of 24."),
("Q29405091","Francisco Maura y Montaner was a Spanish painter born in Palma de Mallorca in 1857. He studied in Madrid and Rome, painted history pictures that won prizes at national exhibitions, and spent his later years in the Basque Country. He died in Irun in 1931."),
("Q10319762","Laureys a Castro was a marine painter born in Antwerp around 1644 who later moved to England. He painted sea battles and ships, and he is known as one of the Flemish artists who brought the Dutch style of sea painting to Britain. He died in England around 1700."),
("Q214074","Claude Lorrain was a French painter born in Chamagne in 1600. He moved to Rome as a young man and spent his life there painting glowing landscapes and harbors in golden light, which influenced painters for centuries, including Turner. He died in Rome in 1682."),
("Q270658","Jacob Jordaens was a Flemish painter born in Antwerp in 1593 who lived there all his life. He worked alongside Rubens and became famous for lively scenes with big, rosy figures, including feasts and proverbs. He died in Antwerp in 1678."),
("Q538350","Maarten van Heemskerck was a Dutch painter born in the village of Heemskerk in 1498. He lived in Haarlem but traveled to Rome from 1532 to 1536, where he drew the ancient ruins, and these drawings are now an important record of Renaissance Rome. He died in Haarlem in 1574."),
("Q548205","Hubert Robert was a French painter born in Paris in 1733. He spent years in Italy and became known as 'Robert of the Ruins' for his pictures of crumbling Roman monuments, and he later served as a keeper of the Louvre. He was imprisoned for a time during the French Revolution and died in Paris in 1808."),
("Q360679","Joseph-Noël Sylvestre was a French painter born in Béziers in 1847. He studied in Paris and painted large history scenes, especially of the fall of ancient Rome, some of which hang in French museums. He died in Paris in 1926."),
("Q2627916","Ulpiano Checa was a Spanish painter born in Colmenar de Oreja in 1860. He moved to Paris, where he became famous for dynamic pictures of chariots, horses and battles, and later lived in France. He died in an automobile accident in Dax, France, in 1916."),
("Q728712","Mór Than was a Hungarian painter born in 1828 in Bečej, then part of Hungary. He studied in Vienna, joined the Hungarian national cause of 1848 and later painted many scenes of Hungarian history. He died in Trieste in 1899."),
("Q215305","Giulio Romano was an Italian painter and architect born in Rome in 1499. He was Raphael's best pupil and finished many of his works after Raphael's death, then moved to Mantua, where he designed the colorful Palazzo Te. He died in Mantua in 1546."),
("Q876701","Ludwig Thiersch was a German painter born in Munich in 1825. He lived mostly in Munich and painted religious and historical pictures, spending some time in Greece, which inspired his scenes of the ancient world. He died in Munich in 1909."),
("Q150679","Anthony van Dyck was a Flemish painter born in Antwerp in 1599. He was Rubens's most gifted assistant, traveled to Italy, and in 1632 moved to London as court painter to King Charles I, where he set the style for English portraits. He died in London in 1641 at the age of 42."),
("Q69708","Charles de Steuben was a German-born French painter born in Bauerbach in 1788. He moved to Paris as a child and became a leading painter of dramatic history pictures, including many for the palace of Versailles. He died in Paris in 1856."),
("Q436726","Ary Scheffer was a French painter born in Dordrecht in the Netherlands in 1795. He moved to Paris as a young man and became a popular Romantic painter of literary and religious scenes, also teaching drawing to the royal family. He died in Argenteuil in 1858."),
("Q311398","Jean Fouquet was a French painter born in Tours around 1420. He became the leading painter at the court of King Charles VII, painted portraits and illuminated manuscripts, and visited Italy, which influenced his style. He worked in Tours and died there around 1478."),
("Q274909","Émile Bayard was a French painter and illustrator born in La Ferté-sous-Jouarre in 1837. He is best known for illustrating books such as Les Misérables, including the famous drawing of the young Cosette with her broom. He died in Cairo, Egypt, in 1891."),
("Q1854159","The Master of Saint Giles was a French painter whose name is not known, active in Paris around 1500. He is named after a famous altarpiece showing the Mass of Saint Giles, now in the National Gallery in London, and he painted richly detailed religious scenes."),
("Q208993","Nicholas Roerich was a Russian painter born in Saint Petersburg in 1874. He painted scenes from ancient Russian history and legend, designed ballet sets, and after the revolution left Russia, traveling through Asia and finally settling in northern India. He died in Kullu, India, in 1947."),
]
json.dump([list(r) for r in R],open("../out/hist_artists_00.json","w"),ensure_ascii=False)
print(len(R))
